  "correct": "2",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\ntan(x + 10°) = cot(3x - 20°)\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\ncot(θ) = tan(90° - θ)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ tan(x + 10°) = cot(3x - 20°)\n\n⇒ tan(x + 10°) = tan(90° - (3x - 20°))\n\n⇒ tan(x + 10°) = tan(90° - 3x + 20°)\n\n⇒ tan(x + 10°) = tan(110° - 3x)\n\n⇒ x + 10° = 110° - 3x \n\n⇒ 4x = 100°\n\n⇒ x = 100° ÷ 4\n\n⇒ x = 25°\n\n**∴ The correct answer is x = 25°.**",
